Negative control for the session pool's per-session logout (parity cell P5 ·
F5 CORRECTED · H9 · AC1.2).

Inverts the cookie-branch in `logoutSession` (`===` → `!==`), the actor-wide
class defect re-spelt against the branched implementation: pressing a
NON-cookie-backed row now takes the actor-wide `logout(actor)` arm (the
cookie-named session dies instead of the pressed one), and the cookie-backed
row takes bare `remove` (the store's write gate re-overlays it — the row comes
back). Every row still renders its own control and the pool still redraws;
the only thing that changes is WHICH session dies. With a single session per
actor the arms are near-indistinguishable, which is exactly why this control
regressed unnoticed and why a suite that seeds one client can never catch it.

The mutant is deliberately NOT a removal of the control: a spec that only
asserts "a logout button exists on every row", or that seeds one session per
actor, stays GREEN under it — that spec was never testing P5.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: session-switcher.spec.ts — the P5 case "removes only the session whose
control was pressed" (two direct client sessions; the pressed row is the
non-active one, so the inverted branch takes the actor-wide arm and the wrong
session dies).

Stays GREEN under it, correctly: the icon-only control's accessible-name and
tooltip cases (untouched), and P6 exit-impersonation where the harness seeds
no cookie (both arms resolve through the same in-memory double there).

diff --git a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/app/components/scope/useActorScopeSelector.ts b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/app/components/scope/useActorScopeSelector.ts
--- a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/app/components/scope/useActorScopeSelector.ts
+++ b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/app/components/scope/useActorScopeSelector.ts
